From e037339cf6e9015327db0f07b3db7cf8dc90fabd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:24:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] druntime interface: runFinalizers, FINALIZE after
 allocation, realloc attributes, profileStats

GC.runFinalizers(segment): runs the finalizers whose destructor lies in the
segment (a library being unloaded) for the allocations of every arena, with
the sweep's rules (no allocation from a finalizer) and with the stock
semantic for struct destructors that throw (FinalizeError). The finalizer is
forgotten first, so neither the sweep nor a later destroy runs it again.

GC.setAttr/clrAttr(FINALIZE) and getAttr: a class instance gets a finalizer
after its allocation (druntime does this when an object gets a monitor, so
that the monitor is freed). A small slab slot has no room for the pointer,
so it goes in a table outside the heap (d.gc.late) that the finalizer pass of
the sweep and the free paths look at; a large block takes it directly. Before,
a monitor was never freed: 0 of 3000 here, 2999 of 3000 now.

GC.realloc: no attributes means keep the block's (NO_SCAN), as in the other
collectors; a plain block is no longer turned into an appendable one by a
resize (GC.getAttr told), and a large plain block no longer reports
APPENDABLE. GC.query/addrOf of a slot that is free in this thread's cache (a
GC.free, or never handed out) say that it is not allocated.

GC.profileStats: collections, collection and pause time, for explicit and
automatic cycles.

-version=Symgc_check_free: stop at the call that frees a slot twice. It
showed that the double free of Phobos' free_list test is a Region copied
by value and destroyed twice (region.d has the TODO).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012fMmy9fJzqrWoKLQjC8Ssf
